# Security

This document records current security boundaries and non-negotiable handling rules. It is not a substitute for project-specific threat modeling, platform controls, or an operating-system sandbox.

## Authentication, authorization, data, secrets, and permissions

{{SECURITY_EVIDENCE}}

## Durable rules

- Never commit, print, copy into prompts, or persist secret values in Plans, logs, fixtures, Skills, or settings.
- Use least privilege and explicit authorization for external writes, destructive operations, production access, and disclosure.
- Treat authentication, authorization, sensitive data, persistence, permissions, and externally reachable interfaces as escalation points requiring an approved Plan.
- Preserve project-owned security tooling and CI. Reporivet does not install a secret scanner or claim security completion.
- Claude permission patterns, if explicitly installed, filter command text only. They are defense in depth, not semantic policy, detection-evasion protection, or an OS sandbox.

